-- ============================================================================
-- RC5 Associate: Reservoir Simulation Essentials (sim/beginner), deep on first
-- delivery (plan of record: petrolord-suite docs/scope/
-- NextGen-Reservoir-Courses-PLAN.md, owner-approved 2026-08-27).
--
-- The structure row is GENERATED from src/content/courses/sim/beginner/
-- manifest.json by gen_migration.py, never hand-typed. Answer keys live only
-- here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no client SELECT policy.
--
-- Inventory: 6 modules / 26 lessons (m01 what-a-deck-is 4, m02 the-grid 5,
-- m03 the-tables 5, m04 initialisation 4, m05 wells-and-schedule 5,
-- m06 the-associate-reading 3), 90 module questions (15 x 6) + 42 final = 132.
--
-- The tier owns READING THE DECK: the six sections and their order, the grid
-- and its TOPS array, the PVT and saturation tables as tables, the vertical
-- wells and the monthly schedule. It grades six quantities that are read or
-- counted from the deck text and never a quantity the deck does not contain.
-- The Professional tier owns the reconciliation against the booking, the well
-- database and the correlations; the Expert tier owns trajectories, the
-- history conversion, the calibration and the validator. This tier references
-- both and grades neither.
--
-- Numeric provenance: every literal is engine-derived. rc5_numsweep.mjs runs
-- the vendored engines through the course's own teaching lab
-- (src/components/course/panels/sim/simLab.js) and sweeps the wave's lessons
-- and banks: 0 unresolved over lessons, 0 over banks. rc5_leakage.mjs sweeps
-- both for a lower tier printing a higher tier's graded value: 0 leaks.
-- The live capstone answer key (applied in 20260828_rc5_sim_course.sql):
--   deck_cell_count 4500 (tol 0),
--   crest_top_ft 5055.774278215223 (0.05),
--   layer1_dz_ft 7.411104817049187 (0.001),
--   swof_first_sw 0.35 (0.0005),
--   sgof_last_sg 0.65 (0.0005),
--   vertical_connection_count 5 (0).
--
-- THE TIER'S CENTRAL FACT: a deck is a description in a fixed order, and the
-- order is load-bearing. Six sections, RUNSPEC GRID PROPS SOLUTION SUMMARY
-- SCHEDULE, at lines 3, 32, 169, 253, 262 and 311 of a 940-line file, and a
-- keyword in the wrong one is a different deck.
-- THE TIER'S SHARPEST LESSON: the deck contains no units. It declares FIELD
-- once in RUNSPEC and every number after that is bare, so a depth in metres
-- in a field-unit deck is a valid deck describing a reservoir at a third of
-- its true depth.
--
-- Bank QA before seeding (recorded in migrations/docs/rc5-sim-pentest.md):
-- length-rank gate green per served pool (rank 0 share 23 pct over the tier,
-- rank 3 share 18 pct, no pool above 27 pct), within-pool Jaccard < 0.50,
-- balanced non-cyclic keys, no em or en dashes, no positional references, no
-- duplicate prompt anywhere in the wave, and no higher-tier capstone value
-- taught at grading precision.
-- ============================================================================

values ('sim', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-deck-is","title":"What a Deck Is","lesson_keys":["l01-an-input-file-not-a-model","l02-the-six-sections","l03-units-and-keyword-grammar","l04-what-this-course-does-not-do"]},{"key":"m02-the-grid","title":"The Grid","lesson_keys":["l01-block-centred-geometry","l02-tops-and-what-they-carry","l03-layers-and-their-properties","l04-star-repeat-and-deck-size","l05-cell-count-and-what-it-costs"]},{"key":"m03-the-tables","title":"The Tables","lesson_keys":["l01-pvt-in-a-deck","l02-pvto-and-the-saturated-branch","l03-relative-permeability-tables","l04-axis-closure","l05-what-a-table-does-between-its-rows"]},{"key":"m04-initialisation","title":"Initialisation","lesson_keys":["l01-equil-and-the-datum","l02-contacts","l03-rsvd-and-solution-gas","l04-what-equilibration-decides"]},{"key":"m05-wells-and-schedule","title":"Wells and Schedule","lesson_keys":["l01-welspecs-and-compdat","l02-controls","l03-dates-and-timesteps","l04-summary-vectors","l05-well-names-and-limits"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward-to-professional"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
